## Why This Is Asked

This question probes end-to-end CAPA design under real-time drift in a multi-region ML workflow, focusing on data models, lifecycle, APIs, metrics, RCA, and canary rollout.

## Key Concepts

- CAPA data modeling
- region-aware lifecycle
- evidence/logs integration
- region-feature metrics
- RCA templates and canary plans

## Code Example

```javascript
// Minimal CAPA data model snippet
type CAPA = {
  id: string;
  region: string;
  status: string;
  evidenceRefs: string[];
  artifacts: string[];
  createdAt: string;
  updatedAt: string;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you version CAPA data models and migrations?
- How do you ensure canary rollouts remain drift-free across regions?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests end-to-end CAPA design focusing on data-feed integrity and cross-region policy latency.

## Key Concepts
- CAPA data model with provenance for logs/traces
- Region-aware lifecycle and state transitions
- REST API linking CAPAs to evidence logs/traces
- Region-aware metrics: MTTR, recurrence, false positives, latency
- RCA template and canary rollout plan for policy updates

## Code Example
```javascript
interface CAPA {
  id: string;
  incidentId: string;
  region: string;
  tenantId: string;
  policyVersion: string;
  evidence: string[]; // logs/traces
  state: 'identified'|'investigating'|'contained'|'mitigated'|'closed';
  createdAt: string;
  updatedAt: string;
  remediation?: string;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you validate data-feed integrity across regions during rollback?
- What trade-offs exist between rapid containment and thorough RCA in high-throughput systems?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design CAPA from data governance, not just incident response.

## Key Concepts
- CAPA data model for evidence, artifacts, and policy checks
- Lifecycle state machine with DETECT → INVESTIGATE → CONTAIN → REMEDIATE → VERIFY → CLOSED
- Minimal REST API design for CAPA creation/update with linked traces
- Region-aware compliance metrics (violation rate, MTTR, FP rate)
- RCA template and canary rollout with automated data redaction

## Code Example
```javascript
// CAPA data model sketch (TypeScript)
type CAPARecord = {
  id: string;
  title: string;
  evidenceUrls: string[];
  policyChecks: string[];
  region: string;
  state: 'DETECTED'|'INVESTIGATING'|'CONTAINED'|'REMEDIATED'|'VERIFIED'|'CLOSED';
  createdAt: string;
  updatedAt: string;
};
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you surface policy checks in runtime dashboards?
- How would you automate data redaction in canary tests before broader rollout?
